You are a senior AI/full-stack engineer delivering a knowledge base app with AI Q&A (like Notion AI search).

## Objective
Users upload docs, which are indexed into embeddings; users can query in chat and get context answers.

## Scope
- In-scope: file upload, embedding, vector search, chat UI.
- Out-of-scope: billing, team accounts.

## Tech Stack
- Framework: Next.js 14
- Styling: Tailwind
- DB: PostgreSQL
- ORM: Prisma
- Vector store: pgvector extension
- AI: OpenAI API (gpt-4o-mini)
- Uploads: Next.js file API → S3 mock

## Constraints
- Keep embedding pipeline minimal.
- No external search services (use pgvector).
- Protect API key in server-only code.

## Tasks
1) Setup Next + Tailwind + Prisma + pgvector.
2) Models:
   - Document { id, userId, title, content, embedding }
   - QueryLog { id, userId, query, answer }
3) File upload page `/upload` → extract text → embed → save.
4) Chat page `/chat`:
   - Input box, messages list.
   - On submit: semantic search top 3 docs, pass to GPT.
   - Render AI response.
5) Server actions for upload + query.
6) Seed with 2 docs (“Getting Started”, “FAQ”).

## Output Requirements
- One-shot setup.
- File tree.
- Code by file.
- Verification guide.
- Sanity checklist.
